  "geometryBasis": "Named mapped Gatehouse and Gaol Block envelopes at their heritage addresses, plus the waterfront building footprint aligned with the Gatehouse stair and corroborated by the Metro Vancouver park records. The three mapped stair flights contain 24, 12 and 24 steps.",
  "sectionBasis": "The municipal Gatehouse heritage review specifies two storeys, reinforced concrete, battlemented towers, lancet and segmental windows and the formal stair. The provincial study and native heritage record identify the stone Gaol Block with mansard roof. Municipal and regional park operations records identify the surviving Wharf Warehouse.",
  "limitations": [
    "The model covers three surviving exteriors and the ceremonial stair. Most of the former prison was demolished after 1980. The original demolished wings, prison walls, burial ground and interiors are outside the scope.",
    "Heights, small facade divisions, facade material colors, mansard and warehouse roof framing and stair landings are estimated from written and geographic evidence.",
    "The original terrain sets the approach and warehouse grade. Nearby river surface, railway, streets and private properties are supplied by the surrounding Earth context."
  ],
